-- allium: 3
-- identity-access.allium

-- Scope: Identity and access boundaries for one personal Vera library and the
--   instance that currently serves it
-- Includes: One sovereign human owner, single-graph instance ownership, the
--   boundary for human and agent participation, stable participant identity,
--   audited reconciliation of accidental duplicates, and the anonymous
--   read-only identity used at a site's public origin
-- Excludes:
--   - Hosting several private graphs inside one Vera instance
--   - Closing the current graph and opening or switching to another graph
--   - Collective ownership; collective work is composed between sovereign
--     personal libraries and belongs to federation specifications
--   - Authentication ceremony and session implementation
--     (see shared-space-access.allium)
--   - Which pages belong to a public site and how they are presented
--     (see personal-site-projection.allium)
-- Dependencies: Participant, Graph and Membership are governed by core.allium

use "./core.allium" as core
use "./agent-participation.allium" as agent

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Given
------------------------------------------------------------

given {
    instance: VeraInstance
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Contracts
------------------------------------------------------------

-- How a person proves they are the person.
--
-- Humans and agents may prove themselves through different authenticators. What
-- remains singular is the Participant at Vera's authorship boundary: a passkey,
-- a federated assertion or an agent token never becomes the author itself.
--
-- What a credential does not decide is the channel. That comes from what kind of
-- participant it proves: agent-participation.allium already holds that an agent's
-- operations carry `agent_generation` and that no human operation ever claims it.
-- A person's credential therefore proves who, and changes nothing about how their
-- writing is recorded.
--
-- The cost of this contract is a real one and is stated rather than hidden: with
-- no unauthenticated way in, a lost credential locks the owner out of their own
-- memory. What answers that is the machine itself — see
-- @invariant TheMachineIsTheLastResort.
contract HumanAuthentication {
    authenticate: (proof: String) -> core/Participant

    @invariant NobodyIsAssumed
        -- A submission with no credential participates as nobody. Vera does not
        -- guess that whoever reached it must be the owner: on a network of any
        -- size that guess hands the graph to whoever else is on it, and a
        -- sovereign memory that anyone can write is not sovereign.

    @invariant IdentityComesFromTheCredential
        -- Who is writing is decided by the credential, never by what the
        -- submission claims about itself. This already holds for agents and it
        -- holds for people for the same reason.

    @invariant TheChannelComesFromTheParticipant
        -- A credential proves who, not how. What channel an operation carries
        -- follows from the kind of participant the credential names, so a person
        -- writing through a credential is still writing, not generating.

    @invariant TheMachineIsTheLastResort
        -- Whoever holds the machine can issue themselves a credential, without
        -- one, from the machine. This is the root of trust of a sovereign
        -- instance: the corpus lives on a disk its owner physically holds, and no
        -- credential can be allowed to stand between them and it. It is also the
        -- reason the instance must never be reachable in that way from a network.
}

contract ParticipantAdministration {
    declare: (owner: core/Participant, name: String, kind: core/ParticipantKind) -> core/Participant
    rename: (owner: core/Participant, participant: core/Participant, name: String) -> core/Participant
    invite: (participant: core/Participant) -> core/Membership
    remove: (participant: core/Participant) -> core/Membership
    reconcile: (owner: core/Participant, duplicate: core/Participant, canonical: core/Participant, reason: String) -> ParticipantReconciliation

    @invariant SovereignOwnerOnly
        -- Only the instance's founding human owner may create access for,
        -- invite or remove human and agent participants.

    @invariant HistoricalIdentitySurvivesRemoval
        -- Removing access preserves the participant's identity on historical
        -- revisions and audit records while preventing further graph access.

    @invariant APersonPrecedesTheirCredentials
        -- A human or agent Participant is declared as an identity before Vera
        -- issues an invitation, passkey enrollment, session or agent token for
        -- it. Those records are many-to-one means of access and authority; none
        -- of them creates another person merely by being issued or renewed.

    @invariant OnePersonHasOneParticipantIdentity
        -- Credential rotation, another device, another shared space and a
        -- revoked then renewed grant all keep the same Participant. A display
        -- name is mutable history and is never the identity key.

    @invariant SimilarNamesNeverMergePeople
        -- Vera may suggest that two declarations deserve review, but only an
        -- explicit act by an authorized human reconciles them. Equality or
        -- similarity of names, contacts or credentials never performs a merge.

    @invariant ReconciliationPreservesBothHistories
        -- Reconciliation appoints one canonical Participant and retains the
        -- accidental identifier as a historical alias. Authorship, grants,
        -- sessions and credential events are not rewritten or deleted; profile
        -- and activity projections resolve and aggregate the alias explicitly.

    @invariant ThePersonalLibraryRemainsPersonal
        -- Inviting collaborators or agents gives them real participation and
        -- never turns the library into a jointly owned account. Collective work
        -- is composed between sovereign individuals; it does not dissolve the
        -- human owner of either person's context.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Stable participant identity
------------------------------------------------------------

-- This is not a second person record. It is the auditable assertion that an
-- accidentally declared Participant names the same person as the canonical
-- Participant. Historical rows keep their original foreign key so the record
-- of what Vera believed at the time remains inspectable.
entity ParticipantReconciliation {
    instance: VeraInstance
    duplicate: core/Participant
    canonical: core/Participant
    reconciled_by: core/Participant
    reason: String
    reconciled_at: Timestamp
}

rule OwnerDeclaresParticipantIdentity {
    when: DeclareParticipant(owner, name, kind)

    requires: owner = instance.owner
    requires: name.trim.length > 0

    ensures: core/Participant.created(
        name: name.trim,
        kind: kind,
        status: active
    )
}

rule OwnerRenamesParticipantIdentity {
    when: RenameParticipant(owner, participant, name)

    requires: owner = instance.owner
    requires: name.trim.length > 0
    requires: not exists ParticipantReconciliation{instance: instance, duplicate: participant}

    ensures: participant.name = name.trim

    @guidance
        -- The participant identifier and every contribution remain unchanged;
        -- the profile history records the former and new display names.
}

rule OwnerReconcilesAccidentalDuplicate {
    when: ReconcileParticipant(owner, duplicate, canonical, reason)

    requires: owner = instance.owner
    requires: duplicate != canonical
    requires: duplicate.kind = canonical.kind
    requires: reason.trim.length > 0
    requires: not exists ParticipantReconciliation{instance: instance, duplicate: duplicate}
    requires: not exists ParticipantReconciliation{instance: instance, duplicate: canonical}

    ensures:
        ParticipantReconciliation.created(
            instance: instance,
            duplicate: duplicate,
            canonical: canonical,
            reconciled_by: owner,
            reason: reason.trim,
            reconciled_at: now
        )
        duplicate.status = suspended

    @guidance
        -- Credentials that historically named the duplicate resolve to the
        -- canonical participant after reconciliation. Their own issuance,
        -- revocation and use records remain attached to the duplicate identity
        -- and are shown in the canonical profile as aliased history.
}

invariant AParticipantHasAtMostOneCanonicalIdentity {
    for a in ParticipantReconciliations:
        for b in ParticipantReconciliations:
            a != b and a.instance = b.instance and a.duplicate = b.duplicate implies
                a.canonical = b.canonical
}

invariant ReconciliationNeverCrossesParticipantKinds {
    for reconciliation in ParticipantReconciliations:
        reconciliation.duplicate.kind = reconciliation.canonical.kind
}

-- The public door has an identity, but not a participant.
--
-- Calling it `anybody` is not a convenience alias for the owner, a guest
-- membership or a participant with fewer scopes. It is the positive identity of
-- an unauthenticated reader at a public origin. This lets the same Vera server
-- and application answer both doors without ever confusing what each may know
-- or do.
contract AnonymousPublicAccess {
    enter: (instance: VeraInstance, site: core/PersonalSite, origin: String) -> PublicReadingSession

    @invariant AnybodyIsNotAParticipant
        -- `anybody` has no Participant and no Membership. Public reading leaves
        -- no attributed operation, grants no corpus access and cannot later be
        -- interpreted as participation.

    @invariant MissingCredentialsNeverMeanOwner
        -- A request without a valid credential is never treated as the owner,
        -- including when it reaches the same server, process or application the
        -- owner uses. Network location and possession of an origin are not proof
        -- of authorship.

    @invariant TheOriginChoosesTheBoundaryNotTheCorpus
        -- A serving origin selects the anonymous public reading boundary. It
        -- does not select another corpus, replica or renderer; the instance still
        -- serves its one graph through Vera, under a smaller authority.

    @invariant TheSameServerAnswersBothDoors
        -- The author's authenticated origin and the public origin route to the
        -- same running Vera server and application. The request origin and valid
        -- credential decide the boundary; no second public server is required.

    @invariant PublicFailureRevealsNothingPrivate
        -- A request outside the public projection receives the same absence
        -- whether the named thing is private, public but not assigned to this
        -- site, or nonexistent.

}

contract OwnerPublicPreviewAccess {
    preview: (owner: core/Participant, instance: VeraInstance, site: core/PersonalSite, origin: String) -> PublicReadingSession
    return_to_owner: (owner: core/Participant, reading: PublicReadingSession) -> VeraInstance

    @invariant PreviewIsARealAuthorityReduction
        -- An explicitly requested strict public preview creates the same
        -- `anybody` session and traverses the same server-side publication
        -- boundary as an external public request. It is not a client-side filter
        -- over data the owner already received.

    @invariant OnlyTheOwnerWhoSteppedDownCanReturn
        -- A session entered as an owner preview may return to that already
        -- authenticated owner's workshop. A session born at a public origin has
        -- no owner to return to and exposes no elevation operation.

    @invariant StrictPreviewIsNotThePublishedMapFilter
        -- Strict preview is a separately named action. The authenticated map's
        -- `Mi espacio` / `Publicado` control changes only its local visible
        -- subgraph and never invokes this contract or changes identity.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
------------------------------------------------------------

enum PublicReadingEntry { public_origin | owner_preview }

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities and Variants
------------------------------------------------------------

entity VeraInstance {
    graph: core/Graph
    owner: core/Participant
}

-- Deliberately separate from core/Participant. There is exactly one anonymous
-- public identity and it cannot acquire a graph membership.
entity PublicIdentity {
    name: String
}

entity PublicReadingSession {
    instance: VeraInstance
    site: core/PersonalSite
    identity: PublicIdentity
    origin: String
    entry: PublicReadingEntry
    previewed_by: core/Participant?
    active: Boolean
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Defaults
------------------------------------------------------------

default PublicIdentity anybody = { name: "anybody" }

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules
------------------------------------------------------------

rule OwnerInvitesParticipant {
    when: InviteParticipant(owner, participant)

    requires: instance.owner = owner
    requires: not exists core/Membership{graph: instance.graph, participant: participant}

    ensures: core/Membership.created(
        graph: instance.graph,
        participant: participant,
        status: active
    )
}

rule OwnerRemovesParticipant {
    when: RemoveParticipant(owner, participant)

    let membership = core/Membership{graph: instance.graph, participant: participant}

    requires: instance.owner = owner
    requires: participant != owner
    requires: exists membership
    requires: membership.status = active

    ensures: membership.status = suspended
}

-- Nobody by default. A submission that arrives without a credential is refused,
-- whatever it claims and wherever it came from.
rule UnauthenticatedSubmissionIsRefused {
    when: core/ParticipantSubmits(participant, graph, origin_id, change, channel, evidence?)

    requires: not exists AuthenticatedAs(participant)

    refuses: "who is writing is decided by a credential; without one there is nobody to attribute this to"
}

-- The same running Vera may answer an authenticated workshop origin and one or
-- more public serving origins. Reaching the latter creates only a reading
-- session for `anybody`; it does not authenticate a participant behind the
-- scenes.
rule PublicOriginBeginsAnonymousReading {
    when: ReadPublicSite(site, origin)

    requires: site.graph = instance.graph
    requires: is_public_serving_origin(site, origin)

    ensures: PublicReadingSession.created(
        instance: instance,
        site: site,
        identity: anybody,
        origin: origin,
        entry: public_origin,
        previewed_by: null,
        active: true
    )
}

-- Esta previsualización estricta se pide por su nombre y queda separada del
-- filtro `Mi espacio` / `Publicado` del mapa autenticado.
rule OwnerBeginsExactPublicPreview {
    when: EnterPublicPreview(owner, site, origin)

    requires: instance.owner = owner
    requires: owner.kind = human
    requires: site.owner = owner
    requires: site.graph = instance.graph
    requires: is_authenticated_serving_origin(instance, origin)

    ensures: PublicReadingSession.created(
        instance: instance,
        site: site,
        identity: anybody,
        origin: origin,
        entry: owner_preview,
        previewed_by: owner,
        active: true
    )
}

rule OwnerReturnsFromExactPublicPreview {
    when: LeavePublicPreview(owner, reading)

    requires: reading.entry = owner_preview
    requires: reading.previewed_by = owner
    requires: reading.active
    requires: reading.instance.owner = owner

    ensures: reading.active = false
}

-- The escape hatch, and its shape.
--
-- Issuing from the machine is not a weaker path that happens to exist: it is the
-- one place where holding the disk is the proof. It is deliberately not reachable
-- over any network, so the instance's exposure and its recovery cannot be
-- confused with one another.
rule TheOwnerIssuesFromTheMachine {
    when: IssueFromMachine(owner, label, scopes)

    requires: is_local_to_the_instance
    requires: instance.owner = owner

    ensures: agent/AccessToken.created(
        graph: instance.graph,
        participant: instance.owner,
        label: label,
        scopes: scopes,
        status: active,
        issued_by: instance.owner
    )
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

invariant OneInstanceServesOneGraph {
    for a in VeraInstances:
        for b in VeraInstances:
            a != b implies a.graph != b.graph
}

invariant PersonalLibraryHasOneHumanSovereignOwner {
    for instance in VeraInstances:
        instance.owner.kind = human
}

invariant SuspendedMembershipCannotParticipate {
    for membership in core/Memberships:
        membership.status = suspended implies membership.participant != instance.owner
}

invariant PublicReadingUsesTheServedGraph {
    for session in PublicReadingSessions:
        session.site.graph = session.instance.graph
}

invariant EveryAnonymousReadingIsAnybody {
    for session in PublicReadingSessions:
        session.identity = anybody
}

invariant OnlyOwnerPreviewsRememberAnOwner {
    for session in PublicReadingSessions:
        (session.entry = owner_preview and session.previewed_by = session.instance.owner) or
        (session.entry = public_origin and session.previewed_by = null)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Actor Declarations
------------------------------------------------------------

actor SovereignOwner {
    within: VeraInstance
    identified_by: core/Participant where this = within.owner and this.kind = human
}

actor AnybodyReader {
    identified_by: PublicIdentity where this = anybody
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

surface InstanceParticipantAdministration {
    facing owner: SovereignOwner
    context instance: VeraInstance

    exposes:
        instance.graph.memberships
        ParticipantReconciliation with instance = instance

    provides:
        DeclareParticipant(owner, name, kind)
        RenameParticipant(owner, participant, name)
        InviteParticipant(owner, participant)
        RemoveParticipant(owner, participant)
        ReconcileParticipant(owner, duplicate, canonical, reason)

    contracts:
        fulfils ParticipantAdministration

    @guarantee OwnerCannotBeRemoved
        -- Participant administration cannot remove or suspend the sovereign owner.
}

surface LocalOwnerRecovery {
    facing owner: SovereignOwner
    context instance: VeraInstance

    provides:
        IssueFromMachine(owner, label, scopes) when owner = instance.owner

    contracts:
        fulfils HumanAuthentication

    @guarantee TheNetworkCannotClaimToBeTheMachine
        -- Recovery is not an HTTP surface. It opens the owner's corpus from the
        -- machine itself, so a reverse proxy on that same machine cannot turn a
        -- network request into an apparently local recovery request.
}

surface PublicReadBoundary {
    facing reader: AnybodyReader
    context session: PublicReadingSession where identity = reader and active

    exposes:
        session.identity.name
        session.origin

    contracts:
        fulfils AnonymousPublicAccess

    @guarantee ReadingProvidesNoMutation
        -- This boundary exposes no operation that changes the graph, submits a
        -- change, edits presentation shared by others, records an exposure or
        -- administers the instance. A write-shaped request is refused rather
        -- than retried under another identity.

    @guarantee PrivateWorkshopAuthorityNeverLeaksAcrossOrigins
        -- Cookies, cached credentials or an authenticated workshop open in the
        -- same browser do not enlarge `anybody`. Every public-origin request is
        -- authorized afresh against the public reading boundary.
}

surface OwnerPublicPreviewBoundary {
    facing owner: SovereignOwner
    context instance: VeraInstance

    provides:
        EnterPublicPreview(owner, site, origin)
            when site.owner = owner and site.graph = instance.graph
        LeavePublicPreview(owner, reading)
            when reading.entry = owner_preview and reading.previewed_by = owner and reading.active

    contracts:
        fulfils OwnerPublicPreviewAccess

    @guarantee ReturningRestoresAnExistingOwnerSession
        -- Leaving preview returns to the authenticated workshop session from
        -- which this owner stepped down. It does not authenticate anybody, mint
        -- a credential or infer ownership from the network.

    @guarantee APublicOriginCannotSeeThisBoundary
        -- The owner-preview operations belong only to an already authenticated
        -- owner workspace. `anybody` at the public origin cannot enumerate or
        -- invoke them, including by submitting their request shape directly.

    @guarantee ThisIsNotTheEyeMapControl
        -- Entering or leaving strict preview requires this explicit owner action.
        -- The eye/map `Mi espacio` / `Publicado` choice never appears here and
        -- never changes the identity of its authenticated workspace.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Answered: people authenticate with passkeys or a federated Vera identity;
-- sessions and invitations are specified in shared-space-access.allium. The
-- machine that holds the corpus remains the owner's recovery authority.
open question "How does Herbert authorize, identify and revoke each agent?"
-- Answered: a human may have several passkeys, while the server keeps bounded,
-- revocable sessions rather than an eternal bearer credential.
-- Answered: collaborator authority is capability-based and scoped to a named
-- shared space; read, contribute and edit are distinct permissions.
open question "When do sessions expire, and what happens to pending agent operations after revocation?"
-- Answered: ownership is recovered from the machine holding the corpus, through
-- a path unavailable to the network. See TheMachineIsTheLastResort.
